== Notes ==
* Sand and other blocks affected by gravity can only be [[Block Swap|Block Swapped]] when using a [[pickaxe]] or [[drill]] with at least 110% [[pickaxe power]], e.g. the [[Cobalt Pickaxe]].{{source code ref|v=1.4.1.1|method=Terraria.Player.PlaceThing_CheckSpecificValidtyCaseForBlockSwap}} With weaker pickaxes, only the topmost block of a Sand column can be Block Swapped with a non-falling block. All pickaxes and drills can Block Swap Sand with other gravity-affected blocks.
* A player equipped with [[Dunerider Boots]] will be able to run faster while standing on any type of Sand Block.
* Sand Blocks (and other gravity-affected tiles) that cannot turn into tiles after falling down will drop as items. 

== Tips ==
* Due to its mechanics, and the fact that it is usually found in large quantities, Sand is especially easy to harvest. Mining any Sand Block supporting additional Sand Blocks will cause an entire stack of Sand Blocks to fall onto the surface below it. As a result, the player can simply hold down {{key|use}} at a single point to harvest a column of Sand.
** The player can simply place down [[torches]] below the Sand column or [[Actuator|actuate]] the bottom row of the Sand column to collect Sand Blocks quickly. Note that due to falling Sand Blocks being considered [[projectile]]s, and the fact that only 1000 projectiles can exist at a time, falling Sand Blocks that exceed this limit will despawn.
* Sand can be used to create [[traps]] for both [[enemies]] and players.
* Like any gravity-affected blocks, Sand Blocks are useful in the creation of safe mining shafts. While digging downward, they can be used to create protective walls lining a cave before actually entering. They can also be used to build walls in [[lava]], which can be useful when building a [[hellevator]].
* By using the [[Sandgun]] with any [[ammo conservation]] bonuses (from armor, the [[Ammo Reservation Potion]], and/or the [[Ammo Box]], etc.), the player can "farm" Sand Blocks by shooting more sand than the gun uses. See the [[Sandgun]]'s page for more details.
* If a player has surplus sand (including biome variants), it can be monetized via [[Glass]], either as [[Ale]] ({{sell expr|Ale|*500}} per 1000 Sand), or as [[Glass Candelabra]]s ({{sell expr|Glass Candelabra|*100}} for 1000 Sand and 300 Torches, or buy the Torches from the [[Merchant]], reducing the profit to {{sell expr|Glass Candelabra|*100-{{buy expr|Torch|*300|raw=y}}}}).
* The player can easily harvest large piles of Sand with [[Digging Molecart]] by placing a [[Minecart Track]], mounting it, then digging the Sand Block next to it and going in this direction at the same time. It will place a track before the sand falls, and the Sand Blocks will drop as items, but the player will suffer some minor damage. Due to the fact that the Digging Molecart cannot mine gravity-affected blocks, the player will have to manually remove solid blocks that are preventing Sand Blocks from falling within the 5 tiles in front of the Digging Molecart.

=== Skyblock ===
* In the [[Skyblock]] seed, Sand can be extremely hard to get. Below are some ways to obtain Sand:
** By Shimmering enough potions from slime drops, Bottles can be decrafted into Glass, then Sand. However, this method is incredibly tedious and has very low yield.
** By Shimmering [[Magic Mirrors]] (obtainable from pre-Hardmode [[Mimics]] in the [[Cavern]] layer) into Glass, then Glass into Sand, yielding 20 Sand per Magic Mirror.
** Putting Sand on the surface of an Ocean Biome will cause various shell variants and Starfish to spawn on top. If sand is under the water it will spawn Shells, Starfish, and coral. These can each be turned into to 4 [[Shell Pile]] using a [[Heavy Assembler]].
** By using [[Obsidian]] or [[Shell Pile]] in an [[Extractinator]].
** From an [[Antlion]]'s projectile.
** Using the [[Sandgun]] with ammo conservation.

== Trivia ==
* Crimsand is the only variant of the Sand Block in which it displays ragged edges in its [[inventory]] sprite, and the only one whose placed sprite is not a recolor of the original Sand Block's sprite.
* There is a joke in the [[Tips|loading screen]] saying that "sand is overpowered", because it is usually despised for its gravity effect and kills with its suffocation effect.
** The same text appears also as one of the [[title messages]].

