== Notes ==
* Just like regular tile conversion, tiles converted by Chlorophyte Ores only got their type changed, they retain all additional features.
** For example, when the Chlorophyte Ore spreads to blocks containing [[liquid]], or [[Hammers|hammered]], [[Actuator|actuated]], and [[Paints|painted]] blocks, the new Chlorophyte Ore will retain these features.
* Despite being mud-based, Chlorophyte Ore cannot convert [[Mushroom grass]] blocks.
* Despite Chlorophyte Ore's tooltip and achievement, it does not need [[Light sources|light]] to grow. However, it visually glows green when exposed to light.

== Achievements ==
{{achievement|name=Photosynthesis}}

== Tips ==
{{for|in-depth farming techniques|Guide:Farming resources#Chlorophyte}}
* A [[Spelunker Potion]] can be used to find Chlorophyte faster.
* When harvesting Chlorophyte, it is advisable to leave small clusters of the ore unmined. With time, they will result in a renewable supply of Chlorophyte.
* Usually it is unnecessary to create an artificial farm for Chlorophyte Ores, since the [[Jungle]] produces sufficient Chlorophyte already. Farming is only required on certain seeds, e.g. [[Skyblock]].
** Since [[Chlorophyte Brick]]s can also spread the ore and do not count into the [[#Limit|ore limit]], farms built with these allow growing more Chlorophyte Ores.
** 1 Chlorophyte Ore can be crafted into 5 Chlorophyte Bricks, which allows building larger farms with the same amount of ingredients. Chlorophyte Bricks can also be [[shimmer]]ed back into Chlorophyte Ores at anytime.
* Chlorophyte Ore is completely renewable due to the fact that [[Dirt Block]]s can be crafted into [[Mud Block]]s. [[Dirt Bomb]]s provide a renewable supply of Dirt Blocks, and [[Stone Block]]s and [[Wood]] blocks can be [[Shimmer]]ed into dirt.
* Turning Chlorophyte Ore into [[Chlorophyte Bar]]s and selling them is {{percent|{{sell expr|raw=y|Chlorophyte Bar|/(|Chlorophyte Ore|*5 <!-- 5 Chlorophyte Ore make 1 Chlorophyte Bar -->)}} -1 round 2}} more profitable than selling an equivalent amount of raw Chlorophyte Ore itself.

== Trivia ==
[[File:Site-logo-jungle.png|frame|right|Chlorophyte Ore inside the ''Terraria'' logo displayed on the [[Official Terraria Forums]] (Jungle style).]]
* The name ''Chlorophyte'' is derived from {{wikipedia|chlorophyll}}, the color pigment responsible for photosynthesis, plus the common rock suffix ''{{wiktionary|-ite}}''.
** The prefix ''{{wiktionary|chloro-}}'' means green, while the suffix ''{{wiktionary|-phyte}}'' means plant; so "chlorophyte" translates to "green plant".
* {{wikipedia|Chlorophyta}} is a division of green algae, informally called "chlorophytes".

