== Tips ==
{{see also|Guide:Farming Resources}}
* Creating a new world and cutting down the numerous trees near the [[spawn point]] is an effective way of obtaining large amounts of Wood.
* A highly effective way to farm wood is to use the [[Axe of Regrowth]].
* Wood has no sell value on its own, but can contribute to a variety of crafted items that ''can'' be sold. Crafting any Wood into [[Keg]]s will yield about {{sell expr|Keg|/14<!--14 Wood make 1 Keg--> round 2}} per Wood or {{sell expr|Keg|/14<!--14 Wood make 1 Keg-->*999 round 0}} per 1000 pieces of Wood. However, much greater profits (about {{coin|5gc}} per 1000) can be had by adding one [[Gel]] for each six Wood, and crafting [[Candelabras]]. There are some conditions here: regular Wood will require a [[Living Loom]], Boreal Wood will require [[Ice Block]]s (as many as the Gel) as well, and Dynasty Wood can do better elsewhere; see the [[Guide:Making money#Crafting|making money guide]] for full details.
* None of the wood block types are vulnerable to [[biome spread]]; Ebonwood/Shadewood/Pearlwood will not spread [[The Corruption]]/[[The Crimson|Crimson]]/[[The Hallow|Hallow]].

