'''Crystal Shards''' are a common [[Hardmode]] [[crafting material]] found in the [[Underground Hallow]]. They can naturally grow on the left, right, and bottom sides of [[Pearlstone Block|Pearlstone]], [[Pink Ice Block|Pink Ice]], [[Pearlsand]], [[Hardened Pearlsand]], and [[Pearlsandstone Block]]s.{{source code ref|v=1.4.5.8|method=Terraria.WorldGen.hardUpdateWorld|field=Terraria.ID.TileID.Sets&#46;CanGrowCrystalShards|t=The actual chances of the growth side are: {{chance|1/4}} left, {{chance|1/4}} right, and {{chance|1/2}} bottom. This is most likely caused by a coding error.}} Due to their constant regrowth, they can be farmed ''(see [[Guide:Farming resources#Crystal Shards|Guide:Farming resources § Crystal Shards]] for details)''. Crystal Shards emit a small glow, similar to [[Demonite Ore]] and [[Crimtane Ore]]. They do not [[Biome spread|spread the Hallow]].

When a Crystal Shard is to be grown, it has a {{chance|1/50}} chance to be replaced by a [[Gelatin Crystal]] instead.

Crystal Shards furthermore have a {{chance|1/2}} chance to be obtained from [[Divine Crate]]s, in stacks of 4–10.

Crystal Shards are also [[Placement|placeable]] in nearly any position (on walls, floors, and ceilings), though they are often not luminous enough to replace other [[light sources]], and placement has no other functional effect. Although natural Crystal Shards can only grow on blocks related with [[The Hallow]], they can be placed anywhere once harvested.

Crafting all items, including only one color of [[Phasesaber]] and excluding consumables and furniture, requires a total of 90 Crystal Shards. The amount required to craft every weapon and every color of Phasesaber is 290 Crystal Shards.

== Crafting ==
=== Used in ===
{{recipes|ingredient=Crystal Shard|expectedrows=17}}

== Notes ==
* A Crystal Shard can grow under the following circumstances:{{source code ref|v=1.4.5.8|method=Terraria.WorldGen.hardUpdateWorld}}
** The source block (on the side or bottom of which the Crystal Shard will spawn) is in or below the [[Cavern]] layer. It does not necessarily have to be in an actual [[Underground Hallow]] biome.
*** This condition is ignored when the [[Remix]] seed is active.
** There are fewer than 2 other Crystal Shards within a 13×13-tile square centered on the target tile. The target tile is where the Crystal Shard is set to spawn, i.e. to the side or on the bottom of the source block.
** Crystal Shards can spawn in [[liquids]] and in front of [[background walls]].
* Crystal Shards are randomly colored either pink, purple, or blue when grown or placed. Their color has no functional effect.
* The color of Crystal Shards can be changed with [[paints]], but the color of the light they emit cannot be changed.

== Tips ==
* Since Crystal Shards emit a glow, removing nearby light sources makes it easier to spot them.

== Trivia ==
* Crystal Shards are fully bright in the dark when dropped or placed inside an [[Item Frame]] or an [[Item Flask]].
* The Crystal Shard is the Hallowed counterpart of [[the Corruption]]'s [[Cursed Flame]] and [[the Crimson]]'s [[Ichor]]. However, unlike the other two items, it lacks a related [[debuff]].

