== Tips ==
* It is possible to obtain Ichor in a world that was generated with [[Corruption]] by creating an artificial Underground Crimson. To do so, one can buy [[Crimson Seeds]] from the [[Dryad]] during Hardmode while in a [[Graveyard]], and use them to seed the Underground Crimson biome, where [[Ichor Sticker]]s spawn and Ichor-containing [[Hematic Crate]]s can be fished. ''See [[Guide:Artificial biomes]].''
** Alternatively, one could simply bring the material from another world which has Crimson.

== Trivia ==
* {{wikipedia|Ichor}}, in Greek mythology, is the ethereal fluid that flows in the blood of gods and immortals, as also said in the item's tooltip. It also means {{wikipedia|Pus|a discharge from a wound or ulcer}}. {{wikipedia|H.P. Lovecraft}}, the creator of the original Cthulhu character, often used "ichor" in his descriptions of otherworldly creatures.
** Although it has no stated color in older sources, ichor is often depicted as golden in modern media, probably explaining why the item is colored gold.
* ''{{wiktionary|ichor|Ichor}}'' is usually pronounced {{ipa|ˈaɪkɔr|before=}} ''{{wikipedia|Help:Pronunciation respelling key|EYE-kor}}''.<ref>{{wikipedia|Ichor|Ichor - Wikipedia}}</ref><ref>[https://www.ahdictionary.com/word/search.html?q=ichor American Heritage Dictionary Entry: ichor]</ref><ref>[https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/ichor Ichor Definition & Meaning - Merriam-Webster]</ref><ref>[https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/ichor Ichor definition and meaning | Collins English Dictionary]</ref><ref>[https://www.dictionary.com/browse/ichor Ichor Definition & Meaning | Dictionary.com]</ref> An alternative pronunciation is {{ipa|ˈɪkəɹ|before=}} ''{{wikipedia|Help:Pronunciation respelling key|IK-ər}}'', which would make the Ichor Sticker's name a rhyme.

