The '''Soul of Flight''' is a [[Hardmode]] [[crafting material]] used to craft several different types of [[wings]] and the {{eil|Soul of Flight in a Bottle}}.

Souls of Flight are dropped by [[Wyvern]]s and are the most common [[soul]] aside from the [[Soul of Light|Souls of Light]] and [[Soul of Night|Night]].

Souls of Flight are dropped at the position of the [[Wyvern]]'s head upon death, and like all other souls, float in midair at the drop point, rather than falling to the ground. This can make Souls of Flight more difficult to spot, e.g. if the Wyvern's head was off-screen or within [[blocks]] at the time of death.

== Crafting ==
=== Used in ===
{{recipes|ingredient=Soul of Flight|expectedrows=16}}

== Tips ==
{{for|detailed tips on the usage and crafting of specific wings|Wings#Tips}}
* Crafted wings sell for significantly more than the Souls of Flight and other materials that went into them, so extra souls are best crafted into wings (using whatever "wing key" items are available) for sale.
* When upgrading wings, decraft the current wings via [[Shimmer]] to get the Souls of Flight back eliminates the need of killing additional [[Wyvern]]s.

== Trivia ==
* Crafting all Wings that require Souls of Flight requires 300 Souls of Flight, meaning the player must defeat 30–60 or {{expert|15–30}} Wyverns.
* The Soul of Flight is one of the few items not affected by [[Items#Gravity|gravity]] (i.e. it floats in midair when dropped).

