'''Soul of Light''' is a [[Hardmode]] [[Crafting materials|crafting material]] dropped by most [[enemies]] killed in the [[Underground Hallow]] in the [[Cavern]] layer or [[The Underworld]] at a {{chance|1/5}} chance. This also includes enemies not native to the Underground Hallow, such as normal Cavern enemies. ''See [[#Notes|Notes]] for details.''

== Crafting ==
=== Used in ===
{{recipes|ingredient=Soul of Light|expectedrows=19}}

== Notes ==
* Crafting all items, excluding the [[boss]]-summoning items and [[Key of Light]], requires 118 Souls of Light. One of each boss-summoning item and a Key of Light require an additional 24 Souls of Light, for a total of 142 Souls of Light.
* An enemy can only drop a Soul of Light under the following circumstances:{{source code ref|v=1.4.4.9|method=Terraria.Content.ItemDropRules.Conditions.SoulOfWhateverConditionCanDrop}}
** The world is in [[Hardmode]].
** The player is in a Hallow biome. <!--
-->{{transclude|Souls|section=common_drop_conditions}}

== Tips ==
* One of the best ways to farm for Souls of Light is to go to the [[Underground Hallow]], and deep underground where [[lava]] spawns frequently, and place a few [[Water Candle]]s. The enemies the Underground Hallow spawns do not go through blocks (except for [[Enchanted Sword (NPC)|Enchanted Swords]]) and are not special in any real way, so they get affected by the lava and drop Souls of Light. This is also effective for any other item dropped by Underground Hallow enemies.

== Trivia ==
* Although the tooltip reads ''{{itemTooltip|520}}'', Souls of Light can be dropped by enemies that are not native to the [[Underground Hallow]].
* In the [[1.3.0.1|1.3]] trailer, the Soul of Light used its old sprite.
* The Soul of Light is one of the few items not affected by [[Items#Gravity|gravity]] (i.e. it floats in midair when dropped).

